(function(){try{var e=typeof window<`u`?window:typeof global<`u`?global:typeof globalThis<`u`?globalThis:typeof self<`u`?self:{};e.SENTRY_RELEASE={id:`40a167f5927668c5c0cb74f2fa9fea4891d58042`}}catch{}})(),function(){try{var e=typeof window<`u`?window:typeof global<`u`?global:typeof globalThis<`u`?globalThis:typeof self<`u`?self:{};e.SENTRY_RELEASE={id:`40a167f5927668c5c0cb74f2fa9fea4891d58042`}}catch{}}();try{(function(){var e=typeof window<`u`?window:typeof global<`u`?global:typeof globalThis<`u`?globalThis:typeof self<`u`?self:{},t=new e.Error().stack;t&&(e._sentryDebugIds=e._sentryDebugIds||{},e._sentryDebugIds[t]=`3027f4f0-bf2f-422c-a872-5d4b5d42f0d0`,e._sentryDebugIdIdentifier=`sentry-dbid-3027f4f0-bf2f-422c-a872-5d4b5d42f0d0`)})()}catch{}try{(function(){var e=typeof window<`u`?window:typeof global<`u`?global:typeof globalThis<`u`?globalThis:typeof self<`u`?self:{},t=new e.Error().stack;t&&(e._sentryDebugIds=e._sentryDebugIds||{},e._sentryDebugIds[t]=`7f9ac764-561c-4f8a-ad4a-7bea0b13f84c`,e._sentryDebugIdIdentifier=`sentry-dbid-7f9ac764-561c-4f8a-ad4a-7bea0b13f84c`)})()}catch{}const e={generic_name:`English`,localized_name:`English (Beta)`,server_locale:`en`},t={copyright:`© 2025 Muyan Studio`,name:`Mandate of Heaven`},n={0:{chapterDisplayId:`Prologue`,description:`Since its founding, the Xuan Kingdom has suffered a string of incompetent rulers. Court factions tore the realm apart, and the Wunu (a northern barbarian tribe) seized the opportunity to invade, swiftly capturing Guanzhong. The capital city of Yong’an soon fell. Royals were taken captive, and countless civilians were massacred. Only the natural defense of the Tianhe River allowed half the kingdom to survive. Sikong Jing, Prince of Langya and a distant member of the royal bloodline, was raised to the throne by the Imperial Chancellor Chen Dao and the powerful noble families, carrying on the imperial legacy south of the Tianhe River. You are Sikong Yao, the emperor’s second son, ennobled as the Prince of Jin. In this age of turmoil, what path will you choose? What fate awaits the realm? History lies in your hands.`,title:`Rising Gale`},1:{chapterDisplayId:`Chapter One`,description:`The Director of the Imperial Academy, Yu Gong, has provided you with considerable support in court politics, but the Chen family falsely accused him of inciting rebellion, leading to his imprisonment. You urgently discussed countermeasures with your two trusted advisors, Chu Huan and Xie Jian'an, and then sought an audience with the Emperor to find a way to resolve the crisis.
Now that the immediate danger has passed, your elder brother has grown hostile toward you. Even if only for self-preservation, it is crucial to quickly consolidate your own foundation.`,title:`Falling Rain`},2:{chapterDisplayId:`Chapter Two`,description:`Chen Dao used Chen Wan'er's rebellious nature to set a trap, seeking to eliminate you before your influence was fully grown. After narrowly escaping death during your harrowing imprisonment, you capitalized on the Emperor's suspicions to cleverly maneuver your way out of the crisis—yet at an exceedingly heavy cost.
Compared to your elder brother, who enjoys the support of the noble families, advocating for the northern expedition remains your most effective means of gaining backing. Now that General Zu Kun has returned to the capital, you must act swiftly to turn the tide in your favor.`,title:`Sea Dragon`},3:{chapterDisplayId:`Chapter Three`,description:`At the banquet, Zu Kun seized upon your dispute with Sikong Zheng to propose to the Emperor a gradual recovery of the northern territories. You, in turn, leveraged Zu Kun's influence to successfully extricate yourself from the capital. 
Now, with the imperial troops marching north, you are like a dragon returning to the sea. This is your moment to hone your abilities and accumulate military achievements.`,title:`Drawn Blade`},4:{chapterDisplayId:`Chapter Four`,description:`Shi Lang's army has besieged the city, and you have led your troops in a grueling defense for several days. Can everyone hold out until reinforcements arrive? Will reinforcements truly come? You don't know, but the incorporated volunteer army has brought you new hope.
Lead everyone to survive. Every extra day you hold the city is another chance to turn the tide of battle.`,title:`Broken Peak`},5:{chapterDisplayId:`Chapter Five`,description:`After seven days of fierce and bloody defense at Yiyang, Shi Lang's forces were finally repelled, and news also arrived of the successful capture of the Northern Frontier Pass at the front lines. However, as the situation evolved, Zu Kun repeatedly advanced his troops in defiance of court orders, giving rise to widespread rumors and drawing considerable criticism within the court.
As Chen Ying's army withdraws southward, new turmoil is about to unfold.`,title:`Heaven’s Will`},6:{chapterDisplayId:`Chapter Six`,description:`With Zu Kun's departure, the Northern Shuo Army marched south, and a new emperor ascended the throne, marking the beginning of the Longwu era in Xuan. 
Over the next decade, winds of change swept through the land, and the Xuan of today is no longer the nation it once was.`,title:`Peace Dream`},7:{chapterDisplayId:`Chapter Seven`,description:`Strengthen the military, revitalize the state, and implement reforms
Now, as the Wuyou advance south in full force, the decision to attack or defend, to stand firm or retreat, rests in your hands.`,title:`Ninefold Unity`}},r=JSON.parse(`{"a00_a009_abe001":{"description":"Thunder and dew alike are signs of divine favor; a suspicious emperor trusts only two kinds of people: the simple-minded who lack cunning, and the forthright who speak without guile","help":"[Prologue] Two approaches → Act according to Minister Xie’s suggestion\\n[Prologue] Relationship with Yu Gong → There is some private acquaintance\\n[Prologue] Presence at the scene → Present\\n[Prologue] Reason for sparing Yu Gong → I wanted to catch more traitors\\n*Not the only way to clear the game; explore other approaches yourself","title":"The emperor's will is hard to predict"},"a01_a028_a007a021_abe001":{"description":"If Wan'er gets anxious, you'll have no way out","title":"Sudden disaster"},"a01_a032_a032033034035036_ahe001":{"description":"Destiny calls—you are the Chosen One!","title":"The Chosen One"},"a01_a053_a012a":{"description":"Every decision here rests in your hands. Try to discern your father's thoughts—speak what he wishes to hear, act as he expects you to","title":"Attain enlightenment and become immortal"},"a01_a054_a012b053054":{"description":"If it benefits my country, I would give my life — how could I choose to avoid it because of personal weal or woe","title":"My surname is Sikong"},"a01_a056_a047048_abe003":{"description":"Emotion, too, is a form of power play. Bowing appropriately now may very well be the patience that fuels your future resurgence","help":"[Prologue] Prince Ning’s warning → I never intended to contend with my elder brother\\n[Chapter 1] The Empress’s pastry → Elder brother, you have worked hard these years; please have some\\n[Chapter 1] Falling into prison → Silent\\n[Chapter 1] Sikong Zheng’s framing → Brother, do you think I would do such a thing?\\n[Chapter 1] Chance to clear your name → Brother, please spare me this once\\n*Not the only way to clear the game; explore other approaches yourself","title":"Dwindling imperial heirs"},"a01_a070_a015c_abe006":{"description":"Hint: Try returning to the\xA0Prologue\xA0and rewrite Guo Xuan's fate","title":"Even I, the emperor, have greed?"},"a01_a075_a064_abe007":{"description":"I suspect you have a brother named Smoking Ascendancy","help":"[Prologue] The Emperor’s gambit → Lose this game\\n[Prologue] Elder brother who erred → Reduce his privileges and order him to make amends\\n[Chapter 1] An arriving army → Lay down arms and surrender\\n[Chapter 1] A word from your son → I will support my elder brother and yield the way to him\\n[Chapter 1] Why mobilize the troops → I have a selfish motive\\n*Not the only way to clear the game; explore other approaches yourself","title":"Decipher the emperor's will"},"a01_a079_a057_abe004":{"description":"Had Guo Xuan lived, today's outcome might have been different.\\nHint: Try returning to the [Prologue] and rewrite Guo Xuan's fate","help":"[Prologue] The scapegoat → Expose her intentions\\n[Prologue] The pawn seeking rescue → Save Guo Xuan\\n[Chapter 1] The path to break the stalemate → The Empress","title":"The Butterfly Effect"},"a01_a080_a029_abe002":{"description":"If Wan'er panics, you panic too","title":"Such is fate"},"a02_a052_a038_abe001":{"description":"our martial arts skills could use some honing","title":"Swords and spears have no eyes"},"a02_a071_a044045046047_abe002":{"description":"Battles cannot be fought with solitary courage alone — it would be wise to find a way to join forces with seasoned veterans","help":"If you do not give Xie Ruoyu the jade comb, the branching scene is triggered from Chapter 2 “How many taels?”\\n[Chapter 2] Zu Yue’s challenge → Spar with Zu Yue to demonstrate your skill and defeat him\\n[Chapter 2] Discussion of the northern campaign → Whether to launch a northern campaign is already settled in His Majesty’s mind\\n[Chapter 2] The crux of the northern campaign → With your elder brother present, such a thing likely would not happen\\n[Chapter 2] Responsibility for defeat → In my view, our dynasty will not be defeated\\n*Not the only way to clear the game; explore other approaches yourself","title":"Lone Brave"},"a03_a034_a007a017018_abe001":{"description":"In war, all is fair — deception is never despised","title":"The Imperial Seal of a fallen dynasty"},"a03_a046_a009a034_abe002":{"description":"War is cruel. Ten deaths are a number; a hundred thousand deaths are also a number — and you must face them with a cold heart to make decisions","title":"He's a real man"},"a03_a057_a045046_abe005":{"description":"To fall before his triumph was won— / Has left a wound in all hearts under sun.' A daring raid with a hundred riders is no feat just anyone can achieve","help":"[Chapter 3] Wu Pu’s main force → East\\n[Chapter 3] Night attack arrangements → Send Zhu Yuanzhi","title":"Poor judgment in appointments"},"a03_a060_a012a054_abe006":{"description":"In turbulent times, human hearts are hard to fathom — it is always wise to tread with caution","title":"Seditious schemes of spies"},"a03_a064_a013a_abe007":{"description":"In turbulent times, human hearts are hard to fathom — it is always wise to tread with caution","title":"Meet one's end due to carelessness"},"a03_a088_a044_abe004":{"description":"Endure humiliation without surrender. Survive in obscurity while awaiting opportunity — bide your time with patience, and let death, if it comes, proclaim your resolve","help":"[Chapter 3] Wu Pu’s main force → East\\n[Chapter 3] Night attack arrangements → Send Zhu Yuanzhi","title":"Emperor Wu of Xuan"},"a04_a003_a001a003_abe001":{"description":"All is fair in war, yet careful thought remains essential","title":"A sudden backward thrust"},"a04_a008_a002a010_abe002":{"description":"Fear not being outnumbered, but fear the collapse of morale","title":"The Carefree Prince"},"a04_a010_a002c011_abe003":{"description":"Two legs, after all, can never outrun four","title":"Frequent Running Champion"},"a04_a011_a002d_abe004":{"description":"All provisions have been transferred to the storehouses south of the city","title":"A fire broke out in the southern part of the city"},"a04_a012_a035_a1_abe013":{"description":"Your martial skills require further refinement","title":"Unskilled in martial arts"},"a04_a015_a014015016_abe005":{"description":"At this critical moment, after much deliberation, Liu Dadao still finds you untrustworthy","help":"[Chapter 3] Suspicion of the militia → Today the people of Wu Pu did not launch an attack\\n[Chapter 3] Acceptance of the militia → Order the militia to break formation and place their divisions under our officers’ control\\n[Chapter 4] Left short, right lacking → Immediately send reinforcements to the southern city","title":"Better you than me"},"a04_a018_a003a020021022_abe006":{"description":"Having signed the military pledge, there is no turning back","title":"The fault lies with this subject"},"a04_a023_a005a029030031_abe007":{"description":"Wait, Shi Lang is tougher than expected","title":"Outmatched in skill"},"a04_a028_a036_abe008":{"description":"Your martial skills require further refinement","title":"Less skilled"},"a04_a031_a038_abe009":{"description":"Your martial skills require further refinement","title":"Showy but impractical martial arts skills"},"a04_a034_a040_abe010":{"description":"Your martial skills require further refinement","title":"The longer the weapon, the greater the advantage"},"a04_a037_a006a042_abe012":{"description":"Even good deeds may go uncredited—let alone misdeeds","title":"So close, yet so far"},"a04_a042_a040_a1be011":{"description":"Your martial skills require further refinement","title":"Backed the wrong horse"},"a05_a012_a003a010_abe001":{"description":"You know there are tigers in the mountains, yet you insist on going?","title":"Brotherly affection and respect"},"a05_a016_a004a012_abe002":{"description":"Can eternal slumber underground also be considered a form of 'long life'?","title":"A fleeting illusion"},"a05_a022_a005b016_abe003":{"description":"Achieving great deeds requires favorable timing, geographical advantage, and popular support. You must pay attention to the timing","title":"Act rashly and alert the enemy"},"a05_a025_a006b_abe004":{"description":"In some matters, either don't act, or act decisively without leaving room for recourse. There can only be one Crown Prince in this world","title":"Hesitation leads to defeat"},"a05_a042_a010a_abe005":{"description":"Lack of patience in small matters can ruin great plans","title":"Refuse to collaborate with"},"a05_a048_a012a_abe006":{"description":"Shi Lang does business with you, but you treat Shi Lang as a brother","title":"Money is no issue"},"a05_a051_a013a_abe007":{"description":"Shi Lang knows the days ahead will be difficult, but you have no 'days ahead' to speak of","title":"Negotiations broke down"},"a05_a055_a037_abe008":{"description":"Cao Biaozhi secured the realm with a single arrow","title":"A single arrow decides the victory"},"a05_a071_a016a050051052053054":{"description":"He loved his realm, but loved his beauty even more. From then on, the empire was divided into three, and who would ultimately emerge victorious remained unknown.","title":"The wheel of history turns"},"a05_a075_a056_abe009":{"description":"Your prestige within the army is insufficient","help":"[Chapter 3] Request to enter the city → Let him into the city\\n[Chapter 3] The imperial jade seal → Host a banquet to receive it\\n[Chapter 3] Northward and return south → When did I ever say I would trade with Shi Lang?\\n[Chapter 5] Heaven’s mandate is with me → The treacherous minister Chen Dao deceived the sovereign; he must be purged and the court must rise against him\\n[Chapter 5] Breaching the city → Flood the city by diverting water\\n[Chapter 5] Evidence of collusion with the enemy → Burn it\\n*Not the only way to clear the game; explore other approaches yourself","title":"Divide and conquer"},"a05_a082_a018a_abe010":{"description":"He who strikes first gains the upper hand; he who delays is controlled by others","title":"Surrounded and annihilated"},"a05_a095_a021b_abe011":{"description":"A sincere heart is truly precious, but that's not what the Chen family wants","title":"Emperor Min of Xuan"},"a06_a032_a007a_abe001":{"description":"Lost in an endless dream, reveling in fleeting pleasures","title":"Emperor You of Xuan"},"a06_a033_a007b_abe002":{"description":"Wine is a poison that corrodes the gut; lust is a blade that scrapes the bone","title":"Emperor Zong of Xuan"},"a06_a034_a049_a1be005":{"description":"The fortune-teller said General Zhu bears the divine aura of kingship","help":"[Chapter 6] Request to grant a teacher → Approved\\n[Chapter 6] The overbearing general → Heavily reward Zhu Yuanzhi\\n[Chapter 6] Rumors in the streets → Find that fortune-teller\\n[Chapter 6] Employing people → Let Zhu Yuanzhi continue to lead the troops","title":"The Imperial Star grows dim"},"a06_a083_a055_abe003":{"description":"Why did Sikong Zheng fail? Was it not because his heart was too soft.","help":"[Chapter 5] Winners and losers → Bring Sikong Zheng down\\n[Chapter 5] Disposal → From now on, do not let me see him again\\n*Not the only way to clear the game; explore other approaches yourself","title":"Emperor Fei of Xuan"},"a06_a086_a018a_abe004":{"description":"Either negotiate with your fists, or listen to the nobles set the terms","title":"Emperor Shang of Xuan"},"a07_a006_a005006007_abe001":{"description":"Long I know in death all turns to dust, yet grieve not to see our lands unite","help":"[Chapter 6] Visit the Marquis of Yongning → Nothing important; he said it was only family matters\\n[Chapter 6] Counsel → Ruolan is a hero of Da Xuan\\n[Chapter 6] Reform obstructed → Grant Xie Xuan Shangfang’s precious sword","title":"Emperor Huai of Xuan"},"a07_a007_a008009010_a010_a1_abe002":{"description":"The Son of Heaven guards the nation's gates; the sovereign dies for the ancestral altars","help":"[Chapter 6] Visit the Marquis of Yongning → Nothing important; he said it was only family matters\\n[Chapter 6] Counsel → Ruolan is a hero of Da Xuan\\n[Chapter 6] Reform obstructed → Grant Xie Xuan Shangfang’s precious sword","title":"Emperor Ai of Xuan"},"a07_a012_a012013014_abe003":{"description":"When the imperial army reclaims the heartland, do not forget to tell your father at the family shrine","title":"Emperor Kang of Xuan"},"a07_a016_a030031":{"description":"","title":"Emperor Ming of Xuan"},"a07_a021_a003a039_abe004":{"description":"He who underestimates the enemy meets defeat; he who fears the enemy faces destruction","title":"The tides of war have shifted once again"},"a07_a034_a008bbe005":{"description":"Unless resolved to fight with your back to the river, do not burn your boats behind you","title":"Emperor Zhuang of Xuan"},"a07_a053_a071072073074":{"description":"","title":"Emperor Jing of Xuan"},"a07_a054_a075075_a1075_a2075_a3075_a4075_a5075_a6":{"description":"","title":"Emperor Cheng of Xuan"},"a07_a055_a076077":{"description":"","title":"Emperor Wen of Xuan"},"a07_a056_a078079080081":{"description":"","title":"Emperor Guangwu of Xuan"},"a07_a057_a082083084085":{"description":"","title":"Emperor Zhao of Xuan"}}`),i={demo:`Demo`,localhost:`Development`,production:`Production`,staging:`Staging`},a=JSON.parse(`{"a00_a001_a001":{"description":"This is destined to be an unrestful night","title":"Prince of Jin of Xuan"},"a00_a002_a001loop":{"description":"Xie Ruolan gives you a precious jade comb","title":"The Costly Jade"},"a00_a006_a002loop":{"description":"Xie Jian'an and Chu Huan differ in their approaches to handling Yu Gong’s anti-imperial poem incident","title":"Two Possible Methods"},"a00_a009_abe001":{"description":"The Emperor is very disappointed with your handling of matters and decides to send you out of the capital","title":"The Emperor's Will is Unfathomable"},"a00_a010_a003loop":{"description":"Should you grease the wheels with a court attendant close to the Emperor to gather intelligence?","title":"The Emperor's Close Attendant"},"a00_a014_a004loop":{"description":"Do you know why I summoned you here?","title":"The Emperor's Summons"},"a00_a018_a005loop":{"description":"What is your relationship with the traitor Yu Gong?","title":"Relationship with Yu Gong"},"a00_a023_a006loop":{"description":"Were you present when Yu Gong wrote the anti-imperial poem?","title":"Whether Present or Not"},"a00_a030_a007loop":{"description":"Since you were present, why did you not punish the traitor who wrote the anti-imperial poem?","title":"Reason for Sparing Yu Gong"},"a00_a037_a008loop":{"description":"Should you grease the wheels with a court attendant close to the Emperor to gather intelligence?","title":"The Emperor's Inner Servant"},"a00_a041_a009loop":{"description":"At this late hour, what brings you hastily into the palace?","title":"Entering the Palace Late at Night"},"a00_a044_a010loop":{"description":"How can you diffuse the Emperor’s anger so you can spare Yu Gong?","title":"Method of Pleading for Mercy"},"a00_a047_a011loop":{"description":"How do you think I should treat a traitor like Yu Gong who disrespects the Son of Heaven?","title":"Dealing with the Treacherous Official"},"a00_a054_a012loop":{"description":"How can you go further and truly move the Emperor?","title":"The Emperor's Thoughts"},"a00_a058_a013loop":{"description":"You are one move away from beating the Emperor; do you want to win this game?","title":"The Emperor's Chess Game"},"a00_a062_a014loop":{"description":"The Emperor asks your opinion about your elder brother Prince Ning’s poor performance in Qingzhou","title":"The Erring Elder Brother"},"a00_a068_a015loop":{"description":"Chen Wan'er claims the truth has been uncovered, but actually the gentry want to sacrifice a pawn to cover Prince Ning’s faults","title":"The Scapegoat"},"a00_a072_a016loop":{"description":"At the brink of life and death, Guo Xuan was probably panicked and mistakenly sought help from your political enemy, Prince Ning","title":"The Pleading Chess Piece"},"a00_a078_a017loop":{"description":"Your elder brother Prince Ning asks if your consolidation of influence means you intend to contend with him","title":"Prince of Ning's Warning"},"a00_a081_a037038039040041":{"description":"You stop and watch your brother’s retreating back as he strides away alone","title":"Walking the Path Alone"},"a01_a001_a001":{"description":"The court is a battlefield without swords","title":"Deliberations in the Imperial Court"},"a01_a002_a001loop":{"description":"Sikong Zheng is proposing to take a Chen family woman as a consort in court","title":"The Marriage Alliance of the Prince of Ning"},"a01_a006_a002loop":{"description":"You and Prince Ning visit the Empress; only one pastry remains","title":"The Empress's Pastries"},"a01_a011_a003loop":{"description":"To foil the marriage between Prince Ning and the Chen family, Xie Jian'an suggests you meet Chen Wan'er","title":"Chen Wan'er's Thoughts"},"a01_a014_a004loop":{"description":"To seek cooperation with you, Chen Wan'er confesses the difficulties of her position in the Chen household","title":"The Eldest Daughter of the Chen Family"},"a01_a019_a005loop":{"description":"According to Chen Wan'er, Chu Huan found the warehouse where the Chen family hoarded misappropriated supplies; it’s up to you to decide whether to deploy troops","title":"Embezzled Supplies"},"a01_a023_a006loop":{"description":"The warehouse is full of arms; you realize you’ve been set up and an elite force arrives, surrounding you","title":"The Suddenly Arrived Army"},"a01_a027_a007loop":{"description":"On Prince Ning’s wedding night, an unforgivable mistake occurred; if only there were a potion of regret","title":"Let the Mistake Stand"},"a01_a028_a007a021_abe001":{"description":"Chen Wan'er’s instigation is utterly untrustworthy! You rush to the palace to explain things to the Emperor; better late than never","title":"A Sudden Misfortune"},"a01_a031_a028":{"description":"Forced to act, you lead your loyalists into armed revolt and break into the palace","title":"Chaos in the Imperial Palace"},"a01_a032_a032033034035036_ahe001":{"description":"Heaven favored you and you succeeded; thereafter you govern earnestly and lead Da Xuan to hegemonic glory","title":"The Chosen One"},"a01_a034_a008loop":{"description":"You were imprisoned due to the Chen family’s plot, and your judge is Prince Ning Sikong Zheng","title":"Thrown Into Prison"},"a01_a039_a009loop":{"description":"In prison, Sikong Zheng distorts the facts and frames you as treasonous","title":"Sikong Zheng's False Accusation"},"a01_a043_a010loop":{"description":"Sikong Zheng urges you to pin everything on Chu Huan to exonerate yourself","title":"A Chance to Escape Blame"},"a01_a048_a011loop":{"description":"For you and for Lady Xie Ruolan, let Chu Huan take the blame and stop the fighting. This is Prince Ning’s last favor to you","title":"The Final Ultimatum"},"a01_a052_a012loop":{"description":"After years of hiding, you have rebuilt much strength, but the situation is chaotic and the front is dire; should you advance or retreat?","title":"The Tumultuous Times"},"a01_a053_a012a":{"description":"From then on, live incognito and be a reclusive couple — why not?","title":"Attaining Enlightenment and Immortality"},"a01_a054_a012b053054":{"description":"Since you bear Sikong blood, you cannot ignore Da Xuan and the people; defend the homeland and do not shirk your duty","title":"My Surname is Sikong"},"a01_a055_a046055":{"description":"Xie Ruolan senses your peril and finds a way to resolve the problem","title":"The Princess Consort of the Prince of Jin"},"a01_a056_a047048_abe003":{"description":"No choice; after all, our father only had two sons","title":"Dwindling Imperial Heirs"},"a01_a059_a013loop":{"description":"When you were in trouble, who did Xie Ruolan seek help from that became the path to breaking the stalemate?","title":"A Path to Break the Deadlock"},"a01_a062_a014loop":{"description":"The Empress is willing to plead with the Emperor on your behalf — this is your chance to allay the Emperor’s suspicions","title":"This Subject Has Something to Say"},"a01_a067_a015loop":{"description":"The Emperor questions why you did not report the Chen family’s misdeeds and instead ordered troops privately","title":"The Reason for Deploying Troops"},"a01_a070_a015c_abe006":{"description":"You suggest that the Chen family took bribes and that I had a share?","title":"Am I, the Emperor, Greedy?"},"a01_a072_a016loop":{"description":"The Emperor’s attitude softens; he no longer suspects your treason so long as you reveal who gave the troop order to end the matter","title":"The One Who Deployed the Troops"},"a01_a075_a064_abe007":{"description":"At least in the Emperor’s eyes, your decisiveness does not match your elder brother’s — go and be a comfortable prince","title":"Decipher the Emperor's Intentions"},"a01_a077_aqte2loop":{"description":"A toast to meeting, a toast to parting forever, a toast to the burden you have taken up. I cannot be the mountain-splitting blade, but I can be the brick under your foot","qte1":"Raise the wine cup","title":"Parting From an Old Friend"},"a01_a079_a057_abe004":{"description":"In the end, you could not wait for a turn of fate","help":"[Prologue] The scapegoat → Expose her intentions\\n[Prologue] The pawn seeking rescue → Save Guo Xuan\\n[Chapter 1] The path to break the stalemate → The Empress","title":"The Butterfly Effect"},"a01_a080_a029_abe002":{"description":"You broke into the palace, but your forces could not overcome the city guard; the effort failed at the last moment — cursed by fate","title":"Such is Fate"},"a01_a083_a069079":{"description":"In this chaotic era there are the extravagant and the patriotic, the schemers and the petty — may Your Highness not forget your original purpose through the hardships ahead","title":"North and South of the River"},"a01_a084_a017loop":{"description":"The power of the gentry and the will of the Son of Heaven cannot be overturned by right and wrong; now you should go bid Chu Huan farewell","title":"The Final Outcome"},"a02_a001_a001002003004":{"description":"When will these stormy waves cease? Perhaps when someone becomes the loser","title":"The Wind Does Not Cease"},"a02_a002_a001loop":{"description":"Xie Ruolan’s younger brother returns to the capital; you and his sister gather at the Prince of Jin’s mansion","title":"A Rare Family Banquet"},"a02_a006_a002loop":{"description":"Xie Xuan and Chu Huan’s entrusted man clashes with someone — do you use this chance to test his mettle?","title":"True Measure of One's Capabilities"},"a02_a009_a007008":{"description":"Speaking of what gift to give Zu Kun, the jade comb Xie gave is rather good","title":"Where Is the Jade Thumb Ring"},"a02_a012_a003loop":{"description":"Zu Kun returns to the capital and invites you to a banquet; how can you leave a good impression?","title":"The Subtleties of Attending a Banquet"},"a02_a016_a004loop":{"description":"Compared with Sikong Zheng’s mountain-like gift, the stirrups you brought seem a bit shabby","title":"A Humble Gift"},"a02_a020_a005loop":{"description":"Compared with Sikong Zheng’s mountain-like gift, you arrived empty-handed with only the breeze in your sleeves","title":"Empty-handed"},"a02_a024_a006loop":{"description":"This rare Kunshan jade finally has a purpose — rely on it to win over Zu Kun","title":"An Object of Great Value"},"a02_a027_a017":{"description":"The scholar who presented a poem to Zu Kun looks vaguely familiar, doesn’t he?","title":"A Scholar's Fervor"},"a02_a031_a007loop":{"description":"At Zu Kun’s banquet, Zu Yue wants to spar with you","title":"Zu Yue's Challenge"},"a02_a034_aqte1loop":{"description":"You step into the courtyard and the duel with Zu Yue begins","title":"The Clash of Blades"},"a02_a044_a030qte4":{"qte1":"Draw sword"},"a02_a047_aqte5":{"qte1":"Charge and shove"},"a02_a052_a038_abe001":{"description":"Due to your poor skill, you repeatedly miss in the duel and Zu Yue is accidentally killed","title":"Swords and Spears Have No Eyes"},"a02_a053_a008loop":{"description":"Zhu Yuanzhi outmatched Zu Yue in the bout; unexpectedly, Chu Huan left this talent for you","title":"Talented Allies by One's Side"},"a02_a057_a009loop":{"description":"At the banquet, Zu Kun brings up the northern campaign — this is your best opportunity to draw closer to him","title":"The Debate on the Northern Expedition"},"a02_a061_a010loop":{"description":"There are countless difficulties with a northern campaign, but right now your task is not to solve those military problems but to resolve the Emperor’s view on it","title":"The Crux of the Northern Campaign"},"a02_a066_a011loop":{"description":"If the northern campaign fails, who dares shoulder the blame for squandering state power? Who can bear it?","title":"Responsibility for the Defeat"},"a02_a070_a043":{"description":"The Emperor seems unwilling to send troops north; if Zu Kun has no objection, this matter is probably decided","title":"Zu Kun's Opinion"},"a02_a071_a044045046047_abe002":{"description":"Because you failed to seize the chance at the banquet to leverage Zu Kun’s influence for the northern campaign, Sikong Zheng suppressed you until you could not raise your head; you had to march north, were ambushed by Wu Pu and died","title":"The Lone Brave"},"a02_a073_a012loop":{"description":"After the banquet, Chen Wan'er brings you a bowl of sobering soup","title":"Sobering Soup"},"a02_a077_a013loop":{"description":"You wish to travel far — when will you return?","title":"Asking About Your Return"},"a02_a080_a051":{"description":"Leaving the capital to join the army and go north, the skies and seas are vast and Prince Ning cannot restrain you","title":"A Dragon Returns to the Sea"},"a03_a001_a001":{"description":"Why would a man not take the Wu hook and reclaim fifty border prefectures?","title":"Northern Expedition"},"a03_a002_aqte1loop":{"qte1":"I, your subordinate, obey orders"},"a03_a004_a001loop":{"description":"On the army’s march north you meet an unidentified youth","title":"The Youth in the Woods"},"a03_a008_a002loop":{"description":"The northern refugees greet the royal army joyfully, bringing the scarce grain they could spare","title":"The Kindness of the Former People"},"a03_a012_a003loop":{"description":"A great battle is about to begin; ask around about Yiyang’s current situation","title":"The Situation in Yiyang"},"a03_a018_a004loop":{"description":"Former minister Chu Maolun of Xuan arrives beneath Yiyang’s walls and seems to want to speak with you","title":"Former Officials of Xuan"},"a03_a021_a005loop":{"description":"Former minister Chu Maolun of Xuan wishes to enter the city to speak with you privately","title":"Request to Enter the City"},"a03_a024_aqte2":{"description":"A mere dog by Wu Pu’s horse dares to request parley?","qte1":"Aim","title":"Execute the Traitor with an Arrow"},"a03_a028_a006loop":{"description":"Chu Maolun says the lost national jade seal is held by Shi Lang and hopes to trade it with you for mutual benefit","title":"The Imperial Heirloom Seal"},"a03_a032_a007loop":{"description":"What do you intend to do about Chu Maolun’s proposed deal?","title":"Northward Advance, Southern Return"},"a03_a034_a007a017018_abe001":{"description":"The imperial jade seal is tempting; you accept Chu Maolun’s words and fall into a Wu Nu trap","title":"Imperial Seal of a Fallen Dynasty"},"a03_a042_a008loop":{"description":"Shi Lang forces the captured Xuan refugees to assault the walls","title":"Refugees Assaulting the City"},"a03_a045_a009loop":{"description":"The refugees steadily approach — under no circumstances may they place ladders against the battlements","title":"The Wall in Crisis"},"a03_a046_a009a034_abe002":{"description":"Never shoot arrows at Xuan’s people! Ride out and fight to the death!","title":"He's a Real Man"},"a03_a049_a010loop":{"description":"To lift morale, you decide to avoid Wu Pu’s main force and launch a night raid on their camp","title":"The Main Force of the Wuyou"},"a03_a052_a011loop":{"description":"This is a near-suicide mission — who will lead the night raid on Wu Pu’s camp?","title":"Plan for the Night Raid"},"a03_a057_a045046_abe005":{"description":"You order Xie Xuan to raid the camp; although the raid initially succeeds, his fondness for battle keeps him from breaking off and the enemy pursues, resulting in the city’s fall","title":"Poor Judgment in Appointments"},"a03_a059_a012loop":{"description":"When Yiyang is in peril, a ragtag relief army suddenly arrives — can this improvised militia really be relied upon?","title":"Unexpected Reinforcements"},"a03_a060_a012a054_abe006":{"description":"The militia enters the city, but a Wu Nu traitor is among them; he deliberately creates chaos and colludes with the Wu Nu army, leading to the city’s fall","title":"Sabotage by Spies"},"a03_a063_a013loop":{"description":"To protect the city, you decide not to admit the militia for now; this will chill their hearts and you must quickly find a way to appease them","title":"Pacify the Righteous Fighters"},"a03_a064_a013a_abe007":{"description":"Sending people out to placate the militia is useful, but a Wu Nu spy learns the Prince of Jin is outside the walls; when the Wu Nu army attacks, you have nowhere to flee","title":"Carelessness Leads to Death"},"a03_a066_a014loop":{"description":"You sneak into the militia camp to meet the leader Liu Dadao privately, but you are discovered","title":"Exposed Whereabouts"},"a03_a070_a015loop":{"description":"To intimidate Liu Dadao you must provide reasons why the militia is unreliable","title":"Suspicion Towards the Righteous Army"},"a03_a074_a016loop":{"description":"To convince Liu Dadao, you must present a reasonable method for rooting out spies and accepting the militia","title":"Recruitment of the Righteous Army"},"a03_a078_a017loop":{"description":"Following the flute’s tune, you climb the walls and find the militia leader’s granddaughter Liu Nian playing a melody alone","title":"The Melody on the City Walls"},"a03_a083_a018loop":{"description":"Are the Wu Pu people truly that powerful and unbeatable?","title":"A Formidable Enemy"},"a03_a087_a070":{"description":"Xuan’s true enemy has never been to the north","title":"Gaze Northward"},"a03_a088_a044_abe004":{"description":"Misjudging the enemy’s main force, the assault fails and you are captured by Wu Nu","title":"Emperor Wu of Xuan"},"a03_a090_aqte3loop":{"qte1":"Put on the cloak"},"a04_a001_a001002":{"description":"Wu Pu has besieged the city for days and no relief has arrived","title":"Trapped in Yiyang"},"a04_a002_a001loop":{"description":"Shi Lang’s army suddenly broke camp and withdrew — perhaps our reinforcements arrived","title":"The Truth About the Reinforcements"},"a04_a003_a001a003_abe001":{"description":"Shi Lang feigns retreat to lure Yiyang’s garrison out, and you fall into the trap","title":"Sudden Turnaround Thrust"},"a04_a007_a002loop":{"description":"Shi Lang launches a general assault and Yiyang is attacked from multiple sides","title":"Struggling to Cope"},"a04_a008_a002a010_abe002":{"description":"Shi Lang attacks from two sides; you decide to send troops to relieve the east. After fires in the south you retreat and Sikong Zheng ascends the throne; you live bitterly as the Exiled Prince","title":"The Carefree Prince"},"a04_a009_a002b012013":{"description":"In the crisis, you decide to lead Xie Xuan to reinforce the southern city","title":"Rushing Reinforcements to the Southern City"},"a04_a010_a002c011_abe003":{"description":"Shi Lang attacks from two sides; you lead the west relief force. After the southern fires you abandon the city and are caught and cut down by Shi Lang","title":"Frequent Running Champion"},"a04_a011_a002d_abe004":{"description":"Shi Lang attacks from two sides; you order everyone to reinforce the north and ultimately die fighting in the south after the fires","title":"Fire in the Southern City"},"a04_a012_a035_a1_abe013":{"description":"You launch an all-or-nothing raid on Shi Lang’s camp but are killed due to lack of skill","title":"Lack of Martial Prowess"},"a04_a013_a035_a2":{"description":"For yourself, your brothers, and the thousands of soldiers who fight to the last, this is a life-or-death battle that cannot be lost","title":"Storming into the Enemy Camp"},"a04_a015_a014015016_abe005":{"description":"Liu Dadao guarding the west fled","title":"Better You than Me"},"a04_a017_a003loop":{"description":"Seven days of defense, arrows exhausted, heavy casualties — Yiyang’s fall is imminent","title":"A Losing Battle"},"a04_a018_a003a020021022_abe006":{"description":"In Yiyang’s dire straits, at Xie Xuan’s urging you decide to burn the granaries and abandon the city","title":"The Fault Lies with Your Subject"},"a04_a022_a005":{"description":"Horsemen into the mountain of blades — return not until broken","title":"Charge into the enemy camp"},"a04_a023_a005a029030031_abe007":{"description":"You storm the enemy camp; an arrow strikes Shi Lang but you are killed by Shi Lang","title":"Slightly Outmatched in Skill"},"a04_a027_aqte1":{"qte1":"Dodge"},"a04_a028_a36_abe008":{"description":"You launch an all-or-nothing raid on Shi Lang’s camp but are killed due to lack of skill","title":"Less Agile Physique"},"a04_a030_aqte2":{"qte1":"Dodge"},"a04_a031_a38_abe009":{"description":"You launch an all-or-nothing raid on Shi Lang’s camp but are slain by Shi Lang","title":"Flashy but Useless Moves"},"a04_a033_aqte3":{"qte1":"Charge and pick up"},"a04_a034_a40_abe010":{"description":"You launch an all-or-nothing raid on Shi Lang’s camp but are killed due to lack of skill","title":"Every Extra Inch Counts"},"a04_a036_a006loop":{"description":"Break the ranks, charge into the enemy, and wound Shi Lang severely — this man will be a future menace. Young one, give your name!","title":"Who Is This Person"},"a04_a037_a006a42_abe012":{"description":"Shi Lang, learning you are the Prince of Jin of Xuan, rejoices greatly","title":"So Close Yet So Far"},"a04_a038_a006b043044045046047048":{"description":"Zu Yue leads troops to relieve Yiyang; Shi Lang is forced to withdraw, and in the southern capital Prince Jin’s mansion Xie Ruolan gives birth","title":"A Joyous Occasion at the Prince's Residence"},"a04_a039_aqte5loop":{"qte1":"Charge and draw sword"},"a04_a041_aqte3":{"qte1":"Charge and escape"},"a04_a042_a040_a1be011":{"description":"You launch an all-or-nothing raid on Shi Lang’s camp but are killed due to lack of skill","title":"Backed the Wrong Patron"},"a04_a043_a039_a1":{"description":"A broken blade does not mean defeat — you can still grab the broken sword. Pick up the broken blade!","title":"Broken Blade"},"a05_a001_a001002003004":{"description":"Yong'an grows distant, our resolve has reached its end","title":"The General Departs"},"a05_a002_a001loop":{"description":"What are you fighting for? And why fight?","title":"What Are We Fighting For"},"a05_a007_a002loop":{"description":"An urgent letter from the capital reaches Yiyang; your scouts sent to probe the capital return at last","title":"Urgent Missive from the Imperial City"},"a05_a011_a003loop":{"description":"Zu Kun has just left; the army’s affairs are chaotic and the capital sends word the Emperor is ill, summoning you home at once","title":"Return to the Capital at Once"},"a05_a012_a003a010_abe001":{"description":"You answered the imperial edict to return and see the ailing Emperor — and never returned","title":"Brotherly Respect and Harmony"},"a05_a014_aqte5loop":{"qte1":"Charge and draw sword"},"a05_a015_a004loop":{"description":"You suspect this edict is not so simple","title":"The Meaning of the Imperial Decree"},"a05_a016_a004a012_abe002":{"description":"You think the Emperor summoned you to abdicate and was killed by Chen Ying upon your return","title":"A Fleeting Dream"},"a05_a019_a022loop":{"description":"A former benefactor now an enemy — persuading Cao Biaozhi to surrender may benefit you both","title":"Urging Surrender at the City Walls"},"a05_a020_a005loop":{"description":"Chen Ying arrives at the Yiyang camp with a ministerial order to take command of Yiyang’s forces","title":"The Ministry of War’s Transfer Order"},"a05_a022_a005b016_abe003":{"description":"You refuse to hand over the tiger tally to Chen Ying; Sikong Zheng grows wary and immediately acts","title":"Alerting the Enemy by Rash Action"},"a05_a024_a006loop":{"description":"Xie Jian'an rushed to Yiyang from afar — this night will not be peaceful","title":"Defying One’s Superior"},"a05_a025_a006b_abe004":{"description":"You refused Zhu Yuanzhi’s counsel and were overtaken by Sikong Zheng’s preemptive strike","title":"Hesitation Leads to Defeat"},"a05_a029_a007loop":{"description":"One step back cannot mean retreat step by step — today we march south with a clear conscience","title":"Divine Mandate Is with Me"},"a05_a033_a008loop":{"description":"After tonight, Xuan will never be peaceful again; those who know your pain wish to keep you company for the moment","title":"The Great Battle Approaches"},"a05_a036_a009loop":{"description":"A thoughtful maiden makes you a calming incense to grant you, at least until dawn, a peaceful dream","title":"Calming Incense"},"a05_a041_a010loop":{"description":"With the passes ahead and pursuers behind, time is tight; a Wu Pu man claims he can resolve the crisis","title":"Pressing Time"},"a05_a042_a010a_abe005":{"description":"Even in crisis you do not wish to trade with the Wu Nu","title":"Refusing to Cooperate"},"a05_a044_a011loop":{"description":"An old enemy met unexpectedly today looks so fallen from grace","title":"Meeting Shi Lang Again"},"a05_a047_a012loop":{"description":"Shi Lang asks you for military supplies and promises to hold back the Qingzhou army","title":"A Business Deal"},"a05_a048_a012a_abe006":{"description":"You generously supply Shi Lang but he betrays his promise","title":"Money Is No Object"},"a05_a050_a013loop":{"description":"It is both business and gamble — high demands, settle on the ground","title":"Haggling Over Terms"},"a05_a051_a013a_abe007":{"description":"Underbidding too hard leads to an irreparable split","title":"Negotiations Broke Down"},"a05_a054_aqte2":{"qte1":"Avoid the arrows"},"a05_a055_a037_abe008":{"description":"In the southern rebellion’s siege battle, Cao Biaozhi’s arrow decides the outcome","title":"Decisive Strike for Victory"},"a05_a057_a014loop":{"description":"Pursuers are at your heels; waste no time — by any means necessary, seize this Tangchi iron city","title":"Breaching the City"},"a05_a064_a015loop":{"description":"During the great battle someone is secretly colluding with the enemy seeking an escape; how to deal with them is your decision","title":"Evidence of Colluding with the Enemy"},"a05_a070_a016loop":{"description":"Eunuch Wen suddenly arrives at the camp bearing the Emperor’s edict","title":"An Unexpected Emissary"},"a05_a071_a016a050051052053054":{"description":"After abandoning the southward march, you bring back the princess, march north and establish a new Jin princely court; the realm is divided into three, and who will claim supremacy remains unknown","title":"The Turn of History’s Wheel"},"a05_a072_a016b055":{"description":"Bold Wen Xian is guilty of forging an imperial edict — for such a crime he should be executed!","title":"A Forged Imperial Decree"},"a05_a075_a056_abe009":{"description":"Many in the army decide to abandon the rebellion in face of rich rewards and high office","title":"Divide and Conquer"},"a05_a077_a017loop":{"description":"Sikong Zheng persuades you to withdraw for now, promising to let Xie Ruolan leave the city","title":"Advance or Retreat"},"a05_a081_a018loop":{"description":"Sikong Zheng demands you retreat further","title":"A Dilemma"},"a05_a082_a018a_abe010":{"description":"You decide to fall back thirty li for Xie Ruolan’s sake, missing the chance and being overtaken by the Qingzhou army","title":"Encircled and Trapped"},"a05_a085_a019loop":{"description":"Winners and losers determine fate; old hatreds and fresh grievances — Sikong Zheng’s life or death now rests on your word","title":"Victors and Losers"},"a05_a088_a023loop":{"description":"The fratricidal fighting with your brother finally ends here","title":"Brothers"},"a05_a090_a012loop":{"description":"How to deal with Sikong Zheng is your decision","title":"Disposition"},"a05_a094_a021loop":{"description":"The secret to lasting prosperity is not putting all your eggs in one basket","title":"A Subtle Blade"},"a05_a095_a021b_abe011":{"description":"The Chen family’s centuries-old prestige — better mutual destruction than letting enemies take power","title":"Emperor Min of Xuan"},"a05_a097_a071":{"description":"Set up an altar, proclaim to the world, succeed to the throne, and change the era name to Longwu!","title":"The Mandate of Heaven"},"a06_a001_a001002003004005":{"description":"Since ascending the throne, ten or more swift years have passed; your ambitions have not diminished an inch","title":"Gazing upon the Vast Sea"},"a06_a002_a001loop":{"description":"On how to deal with Wu Pu, your two sons each have their own views","title":"Tactics and Strategy"},"a06_a007_a002loop":{"description":"The Crown Prince’s horse ran wild and struck the imperial carriage","title":"Startled Horse"},"a06_a012_a003loop":{"description":"State affairs weigh heavily; only with Lady Jing can you find some leisure","title":"Consort Liu Jing"},"a06_a016_a004loop":{"description":"You planned to find peace with Lady Jing, but Chen Wan'er unexpectedly came to the palace","title":"Lady Chen"},"a06_a020_a005loop":{"description":"The treasury is thin — where should this year’s limited funds be spent?","title":"Court Expenditures"},"a06_a024_a006loop":{"description":"It is late — where will you stay tonight?","title":"Flipping the Plaques"},"a06_a031_a007loop":{"description":"This debauched, carnivorous revelry and absurd dream must now be awakened from","title":"An Absurd Grand Dream"},"a06_a032_a007a_abe001":{"description":"My dragon throne, my realm, my beauties — how could a mere Crown Prince covet them!","title":"Emperor You of Xuan"},"a06_a033_a007b_abe002":{"description":"Ruolan, Sheng’er has grown up now…","title":"Emperor Zong of Xuan"},"a06_a034_a049_a1be005":{"description":"You have truly made old Zhu suffer","title":"The Dimmed Imperial Star"},"a06_a035_a050051052":{"description":"Fortunately Zhu Yuanzhi rushed to rescue the sovereign and should be made Grand General!","title":"Grand General Zhu"},"a06_a039_a008loop":{"description":"Reform requires leadership; Xie Xuan has languished so many years — now is the time to use him","title":"Visiting the Marquis of Yongning"},"a06_a042_a009loop":{"description":"Now is the time to have Xie Xuan devote himself and serve the cause of Xuan","title":"Words of Persuasion"},"a06_a046_a010loop":{"description":"Unexpectedly, Chen Wan'er brought her son to pay respects to Ruolan","title":"Paying Respects to Ruolan"},"a06_a050_a011loop":{"description":"Sikong Xu wishes to make your right-hand man, the powerful general Zhu Yuanzhi, his mentor","title":"Requesting an Imperial Tutor"},"a06_a054_a012loop":{"description":"Zhu Yuanzhi grows more overbearing; the military ministry has repeatedly impeached him as disobedient despite his great achievements","title":"The Overbearing General"},"a06_a059_a013loop":{"description":"According to Fan Zhong, rumors say Zhu Yuanzhi has the makings of an emperor","title":"Rumors among the People"},"a06_a063_a014loop":{"description":"Regarding how to handle Zhu Yuanzhi, Xie Jian'an asks your stance","title":"Employment of Personnel"},"a06_a067_a015loop":{"description":"The Eastern Yan requests to marry the Xuan princess as a condition for alliance","title":"Marriage Alliance"},"a06_a074_a016loop":{"description":"Xie Xuan’s reforms end in failure","title":"Failed Reforms"},"a06_a075_a016a":{"description":"Between you and Xie Xuan there seems an invisible wall; apart from \\"let it be,\\" words are powerless","title":"Estrangement"},"a06_a076_a016b":{"description":"Facing Xie Xuan’s perfunctory attitude, you seem to have no choice but to give up","title":"Perfunctory Response"},"a06_a078_a017loop":{"description":"Reform in Qingzhou faces many difficulties; Xie Jian'an asks you to recall Xie Xuan","title":"Thwarted Reforms"},"a06_a079_a017a":{"description":"Recall Xie Xuan — we cannot let him fall into danger again","title":"Ceasing Action"},"a06_a080_a017b048":{"description":"Grant Xie Xuan the Shangfang sword; if a policy is changed, change it thoroughly","title":"Pursuing Reform to the End"},"a06_a081_a049":{"description":"The gentry’s troops are near the capital — will Zhu Yuanzhi truly come to their aid?","title":"Suspicion"},"a06_a082_a053054":{"description":"The gentry’s forces are near the capital, Zu Yue is held up by Wu Pu, and the court is alarmed — what to do?","title":"Restless Fear"},"a06_a083_a055_abe003":{"description":"Your past leniency in sparing Sikong Zheng has now produced this great disaster","title":"The Deposed Emperor of Xuan"},"a06_a085_a018loop":{"description":"The gentry alliance has reached the capital; faced with their demands you must decide","title":"Choices and Sacrifices"},"a06_a086_a018a_abe004":{"description":"What if troops are at the capital? If there must be war, then let there be war — I will not compromise with the gentry","title":"The Ill-Fated Emperor of Xuan"},"a06_a087_a018b057058059060":{"description":"Execute Xie Xuan to divide the gentry; your path must not end here — you must lead Da Xuan onward","title":"Weighing Priorities"},"a07_a001_a001002003":{"description":"Shi Lang has prepared for years and at last musters his great host southward","title":"The Iron Hooves March Southward"},"a07_a003_a001loop":{"description":"Reform failed and state strength was harmed — facing Shi Lang’s southern army, what will you do?","title":"Striving to Respond"},"a07_a006_a005006007_abe001":{"description":"The wounds of failed reform have not healed; retreating to Tianhe is the safest course","title":"Emperor Huai of Xuan"},"a07_a007_a008009010_a010_a1_abe002":{"description":"Even if reforms failed and the state is weak, you do not intend to hand the northern passes to others","title":"Emperor Ai of Xuan"},"a07_a009_a002loop":{"description":"Toil and governance are for the present era; Xuan and Wu Pu still have one last battle!","title":"There Is Still a Battle to Fight"},"a07_a012_a012013014_abe003":{"description":"With the realm at peace, we should not start new wars; to spare the people suffering, retreating to Tianhe is the wisest","title":"Emperor Kang of Xuan"},"a07_a016_a030031":{"description":"This barrier joining Heaven and Earth, built on blood, can secure peace for ten thousand generations","title":"Emperor Ming of Xuan"},"a07_a017_aqte1loop":{"description":"Years of accumulation — all for the day we no longer endure others’ bullying","qte1":"Charge and turn around","title":"March North with the Army"},"a07_a020_a003loop":{"description":"Urgency — Shi Lang breaches the central camp","title":"King Against King"},"a07_a021_a003a039_abe004":{"description":"Shi Lang shoots and kills the Xuan Emperor in desperation, reversing the battle","title":"The Tides of War Have Shifted Once More"},"a07_a023_a008loop":{"description":"Wu Pu is trapped and the arrow is on the string; yet a dispatch arrives from the rear","title":"Chaos in the Rear"},"a07_a024_a008a":{"description":"Chen Wan'er executes a gentry minister to quell the unrest","title":"The Cry of the Luan and Phoenix"},"a07_a025_a004loop":{"description":"Your time is nearly up; you must arrange your affairs before the end","title":"Ruler and Subject, Each in Their Place"},"a07_a029_a005loop":{"description":"You possess countless beauties, but as life wanes you only want one by your side","title":"A Ladle of Weak Water"},"a07_a034_a008bbe005":{"description":"The opportunity for battle can be sought again, but the state must not be lost — withdraw quickly to pacify the realm","title":"Emperor Zhuang of Xuan"},"a07_a037_aqte2loop":{"qte1":"Charge and shoot an arrow"},"a07_a038_a006loop":{"description":"To whom should this Xuan realm be entrusted? You already have your choice","title":"The Decree of Abdication"},"a07_a043_a007loop":{"description":"If you hand Xuan to the eldest, will the second truly willingly assist?","title":"Father and Son"},"a07_a049_a009loop":{"description":"You ask your ministers whom they think should succeed you","title":"Who Shall Bear the Great Responsibility"},"a07_a050_a066067068":{"description":"Guard the land and open new frontiers — what is one life to that?","title":"The Nine Provinces United as One"},"a07_a053_a071072073074":{"description":"Let Sheng’er rule while Xu’er assists; our Sikong household must no longer be stained by kin’s blood","title":"Emperor Jing of Xuan"},"a07_a054_a075075_a1075_a2075_a3075_a4075_a5075_a6":{"description":"In an imperial house there is no room for family sentiment. To ensure Sikong Sheng’s smooth succession, you decide to poison your younger son","title":"Emperor Cheng of Xuan"},"a07_a055_a076077":{"description":"The state rises by martial strength; with Xu’er and General Zhu supporting each other, Da Xuan can be at peace","title":"Emperor Wen of Xuan"},"a07_a056_a010loop":{"description":"Not knowing how it began, yet falling in deep","title":"A Pair of Lovebirds"},"a07_a056_a078079080081":{"description":"A benevolent ruler and good ministers entrust the realm to Sheng’er and General Zu Yue; there will be no worries","title":"Emperor Guangwu of Xuan"},"a07_a057_a082083084085":{"description":"Balance is the art of power — but sometimes it goes too far","title":"Emperor Zhao of Xuan"},"a07_a061_a011loop":{"description":"Grudges and favors entwined","title":"Intertwined Branches"},"a07_a065_a012loop":{"description":"Together forever, together longing","title":"A Pair of Flying Swallows"},"a07_a070_aqte3loop":{"qte1":"View the afterword"}}`),o=JSON.parse(`{"刘大刀":{"description":"Leader of the northern fortress clans and commander of the righteous army, once a soldier in the Yongan army.\\nDuring the Wu invasion, fear drove him to desert. Later, he learned his wife and son perished in flight, plunging him into grief and remorse. After his daughter-in-law’s death, he raised his granddaughter Liu Nian alone, the two depending solely on each other.","name":"Liu Dadao"},"刘念":{"description":"Granddaughter of Liu Dadao, leader of the northern fortress clans.\\nOrphaned young, she grew up under her grandfather’s care in the lost northern lands, enduring hardship. Having witnessed countless friends and kin slain by the Wunu, she longs for the day when the people of the north can live in peace again.","name":"Liu Nian"},"司空旭":{"description":"Second son of Sikong Yao and Chen Waner, titled Prince of Yan.\\nSupported by his mother, the leading voice of the Chen family, and admired by General Zhu Yuanzhi, he is forthright, bold, and valiant. His reputation is strong both in the army and among the nobility.","name":"Sikong Xu"},"司空景":{"description":"Originally a collateral member of the royal family, titled Prince of Langya. When the Wunu invaders pressed south and the capital Yongan City fell, he retreated south and, with the backing of the Chen family and allied noble families, was enthroned as the new Emperor.\\nObsessed with alchemy and mysticism, he left state affairs largely in the hands of the nobility.","name":"Sikong Jing"},"司空正":{"description":"Eldest son of Emperor Sikong Jing, titled Prince of Ning.\\nAs the first son of the Prince of Langya, he bore concern for the realm and often protected his younger brother. After the southern retreat, he grew close to the Chen family and came to advocate a policy of cautious defense. Thus, in court, his views diverged from those of Sikong Yao, and the two brothers gradually drifted apart.","name":"Sikong Zheng"},"司空盛":{"description":"Eldest son of Sikong Yao and Xie Ruolan, titled Crown Prince of Xuan.\\nIn childhood, he lived through his father’s struggle for the throne and his mother’s death. Entrusted with high hopes by his father, he was raised with respect and discipline. Polished and diligent, just as his mother had wished, he grew into a prince of great talent for governance, devoted to aiding his father and caring for the people.","name":"Sikong Sheng"},"司空耀":{"description":"Second son of Emperor, Sikong Jing of Great Xuan, titled Prince of Jin.\\nIn his youth, he lived through the turmoil of the southern retreat and often mingled in army camps. After receiving his title, he appointed talents regardless of origin, welcomed heroes from all walks of life, and heavily funded artisans in the Office of Works. He oversaw several improvements in weaponry and military equipment, earning high prestige both among the people and the army.","name":"Sikong Yao"},"司空钰":{"description":"Youngest daughter of Sikong Yao, born of Liu Nian, titled Princess of Xunyang.\\nIt is said that at her birth, magnolia trees in the palace bloomed in splendor. Delighted, the Emperor personally named her “Yu,” likening her to flawless jade, precious beyond compare.\\nCherished deeply by the Emperor and his consort since childhood, she grew not arrogant but graceful, lively, and kind. Between her elder brothers, Crown Prince, Sikong Sheng and Prince of Yan, Sikong Xu—both renowned yet at odds in politics—she mediates with sincerity and innocence. At imperial banquets, her words often ease tensions, and though the brothers are bitter rivals, both dote on their younger sister.","name":"Sikong Yu"},"曹表之":{"description":"A direct heir of the Cao family of Xuan, serving as Vice-Minister of Revenue. Though born into one of the top noble families, he is upright and unyielding, disdaining empty ritual. He often sheds his silks for plain robes, mingling with merchants and commoners, drinking alongside roving swordsmen, and gathering the latest intelligence from across the realm.","name":"Cao Biaozhi"},"朱元之":{"description":"Of humble origins and blessed with immense strength, he spent his childhood forging iron, raiding, and working as a mercenary in the north with his father. After their bandit lair was destroyed by the Wu, he fled south alone. Later, when he waylaid Chu Huan’s carriage, his talent was recognized and he was taken in as a follower, joining the army to hone his skills.","name":"Zhu Yuanzhi"},"李定远":{"description":"Commander of Imperial City Guard. Skilled at reading people, he has connections both in the light and the shadows. Quick to gather intelligence, he has twice switched allegiance, serving two successive emperors as spymaster.","name":"Li Dingyuan"},"林戍":{"description":"Once a frontier hero who gathered followers for protection in the war-torn borderlands. When he heard that Zu Kun was leading troops north, he brought his men to join and humbly requested to serve as a mere foot soldier. Zu Kun placed him under Sikong Yao’s command at Yiyang.\\nTaciturn yet fierce, he always fought at the front lines. In the bloody defense of Yiyang, he and Zhu Yuanzhi held the northern wall, where he witnessed Shi Lang’s command banner fall. From then on, he pledged himself wholly to Prince of Jin. Rising from outlaw to general through countless campaigns, he remained steadfast and loyal. Despite his high rank, he lived simply, often standing with his hand on his sword at the palace steps, guarding the Emperor’s carriage.","name":"Lin Shu"},"柳才人":{"description":"Orphaned as a child, she was adopted by nobles and trained in song and dance. Later presented to the Emperor, her unmatched beauty and natural allure captivated him, winning her favor and indulgence for a time.","name":"Consort Liu"},"楚桓":{"description":"Once a trusted retainer of Emperor Sikong Jing, now the closest aide to Sikong Yao. He once led troops to protect Sikong Jing’s family during their retreat south. Loyal and righteous, he deeply supports Sikong Yao’s ambition to reclaim the north.\\nTo Sikong Yao, he is both a loyal subject and a guardian who cared for him since childhood.","name":"Chu Huan"},"楚茂伦":{"description":"Once the governor of Shuoyang prefecture in Xuan. To protect his wife and daughters, he betrayed the realm and defected to the Wu, becoming a strategist under General Shi Lang.","name":"Chu Maolun"},"楚蒙":{"description":"Son of Chu Huan. When his father was accused, Prince of Jin secretly protected him by changing his name and placing him in the army. After Prince of Jin ascended the throne, he was promoted to Captain of the Imperial Guard. To the court, he seemed taciturn and awkward, yet he held the Emperor’s special favor. Whenever the Emperor toured, Chu Meng was always three steps behind.","name":"Chu Meng"},"王寡妇":{"description":"No one knows her real name—everyone calls her Widow Wang. It is said she was once the daughter of a wealthy merchant. On her wedding day, her household was destroyed by Wu raiders, forcing her into exile.\\nYears of hardship hardened her tongue, making her sharp and formidable, often intimidating her companions. Yet her heart still bore kindness: when she saw the helpless, she would share her food, even as she cursed them.\\nShe had seen the royal army march north and offered her grain in welcome. She had survived the Wu massacres, falling into valleys and living on wild fruit. She had stood at Yiyang’s gates to watch the Emperor return in triumph. She endured the decline of Xuan and now witnessed the rise of Great Xuan. Hers was a life of sixty turbulent, extraordinary years…\\nOr so she claims. Now, in the taverns of the southern capital, crowds gather daily to hear this woman storyteller spin her tales anew.","name":"Widow Wang"},"王明":{"description":"Born the son of commoners, he grew up in poverty. In his youth, he earned a living by writing essays for wealthy households. The integrity and spirit within his words caught the eye of Yu Gong, who applauded his talent and sought him out, taking him as a disciple.\\nWith Yu Gong’s guidance, Wang Ming became upright and disciplined. Yu Gong often jested with Prince Jin, saying, This boy is much like I was in my youth.","name":"Wang Ming"},"皇后李氏":{"description":"Formerly Princess Consort of Langya, she was made Empress of Xuan after the southern retreat. Dignified and gentle, she never intervenes in state affairs. Mother of both Sikong Zheng and Sikong Yao, she shows deep affection for her two sons.","name":"Empress Li"},"石狼":{"description":"Right General of the Wu.\\nA fierce and battle-hardened warrior who earned repeated merit in the southern campaigns. Yet because his mother was a captured slave, his lowly birth left him scorned and marginalized among the Wu aristocracy.","name":"Shi Lang"},"祖坤":{"description":"A native of Yongan City, Great General of Xuan and pillar of the realm, the chief commander guarding the Tianhe front against the Wu.\\nSteady and mature, calm in judgment and never revealing his emotions, he has repelled the Wu’s invasions many times and enjoys immense prestige within the army. Rarely meddling in politics, he is often praised for his integrity.","name":"Zu Kun"},"祖月":{"description":"Daughter of Great General Zu Kun of Xuan. Having followed her father on campaigns for years, she became a formidable warrior with an open and lively spirit. In private, she sometimes longed for the splendor of Jiangnan’s pavilions and admired cultured scholars and handsome men.\\nYet life in the army also shaped her into someone decisive and ruthless in serious matters. When carrying out orders, she never allowed personal feelings, striking fear into her enemies.","name":"Zu Yue"},"福江":{"description":"Born a refugee, he endured illness and hunger in youth. Determined to rise above his station, he enlisted under Sikong Yao.\\nYet in the perilous struggle for power, he was deceived by Chen Ying and swayed by profit and fear into betrayal. Never did he imagine Chen Ying would fall in a mutiny. One wrong step erased all his past merits. When the blade pierced his chest, his eyes widened in shock and disbelief.","name":"Fu Jiang"},"虞宫":{"description":"Born to a noble family, he gained fame early for his learning. Repeatedly promoted by the court, he served as Chancellor of the Imperial Academy and even lectured the young Prince of Jin.\\nDespite his lofty position, he bore no prejudice of birth and recommended many upright talents to Prince Sikong Yao, dedicated to reviving Xuan and serving the people. His disciples and associates fill the court. Free-spirited and unrestrained, his only weakness is drink—at every cup he drinks, by the third he is always drunk.","name":"Yu Gong"},"谢建安":{"description":"Head of the noble Xie family of Danling, in-law and trusted aide of Prince of Jin, Sikong Yao.\\nA shrewd and calculating strategist, he often resorts to ruthless means to achieve his goals. Politically, he supports Sikong Yao with full effort, yet he also pursues schemes for the benefit of his own family.","name":"Xie Jianan"},"谢玄":{"description":"Younger brother of Princess Consort, Xie Ruolan, from the illustrious Xie family. Known across Xuan as a charming and flamboyant rake, he now serves under General Zu Kun for experience, though he retains his carefree nature. Whenever he rides through the bustling streets clad in silver armour, courtesans lean from the balconies, waving their sleeves in flirtation.","name":"Xie Xuan"},"谢若兰":{"description":"Daughter of the noble Xie family of Danling, Princess Consort of Prince of Jin, Sikong Yao.\\nGifted in dance, music, and calligraphy, she grew up in the south, cherished by her father and brothers, famed as the “Pearl of Danling.” After her marriage, she became even more treasured by the Prince, serving as the vital bridge between Sikong Yao and the Xie family.","name":"Xie Ruolan"},"赵武":{"description":"A minor officer in the army, neither outstanding nor faulty, he marched south with Sikong Yao. Yet doubt grew in his heart. When the army was stalled at Dongming City, he secretly wrote a surrender letter to the enemy, which was discovered, leading to his dismissal.He laid down his arms and returned to the fields, living as a farmer. In his old age, when he suddenly heard the Emperor was touring his hometown, he stood trembling with his cane behind his thatched gate. At the sound of drums and gongs, he covered his face and retreated into his hut, ashamed to look upon the imperial presence.","name":"Zhao Wu"},"邱胜":{"description":"Sworn brother of Liu Dadao, leader of the northern righteous army. Wielding a long spear, he is unmatched in battle. Fiery by nature, he scorns the Wu’s repeated attempts to win him over.","name":"Qiu Sheng"},"陈婉儿":{"description":"Daughter of the Chen family, the greatest noble family in Xuan. After the death of her parents, power shifted to her great-uncle Chen Dao, and her branch of the family was gradually stripped of influence.\\nAs the last daughter of the main line, she refused to let her uncle dictate her fate. Pushed out of the family’s center of power, she relied on her intelligence and wit to maneuver among factions and secure advantages for herself.","name":"Chen Waner"},"陈导":{"description":"Chancellor of Xuan and head of the powerful Chen family, the foremost noble family of the realm. Deeply calculating, treacherous, and ruthless, he foresaw the turmoil that would follow the princes’ struggles and the Wunu invasion. He chose to back the reclusive Prince of Langya and rose to dominance as the leading noble in the south.","name":"Chen Dao"},"陈应":{"description":"Son of Chancellor Chen Dao, who helps his father control part of the military. Born into privilege and wielding great power, he is arrogant, cruel, and debauched.","name":"Chen Ying"},"雅儿":{"description":"A tribute girl from a small western kingdom, blessed with ivory skin and stunning beauty. Though unskilled in the music of the Central Plains upon entering the palace, her exotic looks drew the Emperor’s gaze. Under Consort Liu’s tutelage, she shed her innocence, and with her fiery and uninhibited charms, became uniquely favored.","name":"Yaer"},"齐九":{"description":"Of humble soldierly origin, once a mere footman under General Zu Kun. Later assigned to serve with Prince of Jin, Sikong Yao at Yiyang, he fought side by side with the Prince, even leading a daring raid on Shi Lang’s camp.\\nAfter Zu Kun’s death, he joined Sikong Yao’s Northern Shuo Army, often charging as vanguard, loyal without fail. With the founding of the new dynasty, he was honored as a founding general, yet still bore his iron halberd guarding the palace gates.","name":"Qi Jiu"}}`),s={achievements:`Achievements`,album:`Album`,announcements:`Announcements`,back:`Back`,chapters:`Chapter Selection`,character_intro:`Characters Introduction`,character_stories:`Character Stories`,character_story_locked:`Locked`,close_dialog:`Close`,continue_game:`Continue Story`,credits:`Credits`,current_progress:`Current Progress`,enter_chapter:`Enter Chapter`,error_initial_sync:`Login failed: {error}. Please check for your Internet connection.`,error_network:`Network error: {error}. Please check your Internet connection.`,help_spoiler_warning:`Help may contain spoilers. Do you want to view it?`,license:`EULA`,load_game:`Continue Story`,loading:`Loading…`,main_menu:`Main Menu`,mute:`Mute`,new_game:`Start Story`,next:`Jump to Next Video`,next_chapter:`Enter Next Chapter`,pause:`Pause`,play:`Play`,portfolios:`Portfolios`,progress_bar:`Progress`,qte_drag:`Drag along the track`,qte_slide_left:`Slide left`,qte_slide_right:`Slide right`,quit:`Exit`,rate_select:`Playback Speed`,reset_game:`Start from the Beginning`,settings:`Settings`,storyline:`Storyline`,storyline_help:`Storyline Help`,test_version_warning:`Internal testing version, not representative of final quality.`,to_storyline:`Back to storyline`,ui_language:`Language`,video_list:`Video List`,volume_bgm:`Background Music Volume`,volume_efx:`Effects Volume`,volume_main:`Main Volume`,volume_video:`Video Volume`},c={军心:`Army morale`,司空正的愧疚:`Sikong Zheng's Guilt`,朱元之的忠心:`Zhu Yuanzhi’s loyalty`,祖坤好感度:`Zu Kun’s favor`,老皇帝的认可度:`The Emperor's Trust`};var l={_meta:e,branding:t,chapters:n,endings:r,environments:i,nodes:a,portfolios:o,ui:s,values:c};export{e as _meta,t as branding,n as chapters,l as default,r as endings,i as environments,a as nodes,o as portfolios,s as ui,c as values};
